This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is shard 'c' of fold-architect-ledger-join-mutants, and it inherits that fixture's reason
without restating it: it is the MUTATION BATTERY behind the shipped fold-architect-ledger-join
fixture, editing copies of core's own sources in temp trees, so every verdict is a question
about whether THIS repository's gate still discriminates.

A shard is a scheduling boundary, never a subject boundary, so it can carry no ship decision
its sibling does not. On a consumer it would be a unit the consumer cannot act on, sitting in
that consumer's suite schedule.
